==Latin==
{{wikipedia|Latin profanity#Mentula and verpa: the penis|''Verpa''- Latin profanity}}

===Etymology===
Probably related to something "thrust" or "thrown". Confer the Dutch {{term|werpen}}, the Danish {{term|verfe|lang=da}}, Icelandic {{term|verpa||to throw|lang=is}} and Faroese {{term|verpa|lang=fo}}.

===Noun===
'''verpa''' {{f}} (genitive: '''[[verpae]])

# {{vulgar|lang=la}} a [[penis]], a [[dick]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|a penis}} [[mentula#Latin|mentula]], [[penis#Latin|penis]]

====Related terms====
* [[verpus]] {{m}} (genitive: [[verpi]]) - "a circumcised man"
*: ''Vos Veraniolo meo et Fabullo''
*: '''''verpus''' praeposuit Priapus ille?''
*:: Did that '''dick''', that Priapus, prefer you to my dear Veraniolus and Fabullus?
*: ''Quaesitum ad [[fons#Latin|fontem]] solos deducere '''verpos'''.''
*:: To guide only the '''circumcised''' to the [[fountain]] that they seek.

